# The RDFS entailment ruleset as Notation3 — the rule text under test by the
# `sq-zgbso.6` SPIKE (`examples/rdfs_n3_spike.rs`, epic sq-zgbso / issue #1582).
#
# MEASUREMENT ARTEFACT, NOT A SHIPPING PATH. Nothing in the crate reads this file
# except the spike example; `Profile::Rdfs` continues to run the hand-optimized
# id-level materializer in `src/rdfs.rs`. Whether these rules ever replace that code
# is exactly the question the spike's measured verdict answers.
#
# Scope: the SAME six rules `src/rdfs.rs` implements — rdfs2/3/5/7/9/11 of RDF 1.1
# Semantics §9.2.1. Everything else that regime defines (rdfs1, rdfs4a/b, rdfs6, rdfs8,
# rdfs10, rdfs12, rdfs13 and the axiomatic triples) is absent here because it is absent
# there; of those, src/rdfs.rs's module docs call out rdfs4a/4b, rdfs6, rdfs8, rdfs10
# and rdfs13 as deliberately omitted, "true but useless, and they blow up the store by
# O(terms)". A spike that compared a DIFFERENT rule set against the materializer would
# measure nothing, so the omissions are mirrored exactly.
#
# Every rule here is a plain Horn rule over triple patterns: no builtins, no negation,
# no existentials — comfortably inside the compiled evaluator's documented subset
# (`src/n3/compiled.rs` module docs), so the spike measures evaluation, not coverage.

@prefix rdf:  <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .

# rdfs2 — domain typing:      (p domain c), (s p o) ⊢ (s type c)
{ ?p rdfs:domain ?c . ?s ?p ?o } => { ?s rdf:type ?c } .

# rdfs3 — range typing:       (p range c), (s p o) ⊢ (o type c)
{ ?p rdfs:range ?c . ?s ?p ?o } => { ?o rdf:type ?c } .

# rdfs5 — subPropertyOf transitivity: (p sp q), (q sp r) ⊢ (p sp r)
{ ?p rdfs:subPropertyOf ?q . ?q rdfs:subPropertyOf ?r } => { ?p rdfs:subPropertyOf ?r } .

# rdfs7 — subPropertyOf rewrite:      (p sp q), (s p o) ⊢ (s q o)
{ ?p rdfs:subPropertyOf ?q . ?s ?p ?o } => { ?s ?q ?o } .

# rdfs9 — subClassOf typing:          (c sc d), (s type c) ⊢ (s type d)
{ ?c rdfs:subClassOf ?d . ?s rdf:type ?c } => { ?s rdf:type ?d } .

# rdfs11 — subClassOf transitivity:   (c sc d), (d sc e) ⊢ (c sc e)
{ ?c rdfs:subClassOf ?d . ?d rdfs:subClassOf ?e } => { ?c rdfs:subClassOf ?e } .
